## 🎯 Mandatory Patterns

### File Structure
```
modules/{module-name}/
├── {module}-controller.go
├── {module}-service.go
├── {module}-repository.go
└── {module}-routes.go
```

### Error Handling
```go
// ALWAYS use these patterns
return utils.Error(c, fiber.StatusBadRequest, "Data tidak valid")
return utils.Success(c, "Berhasil dibuat", 201, data)
```

### Response Format
- Success: Use `utils.Success()`
- Error: Use `utils.Error()`
- Messages MUST be in Bahasa Indonesia

### Naming Conventions
- Interfaces: `I{Module}Service`, `I{Module}Repository`
- Structs: `{Module}Controller`, `{module}Service`
- Functions: Follow existing patterns in similar modules

## 🔧 Technical Requirements

### Framework
- **ONLY use Go Fiber** (NO Gin or other frameworks)
- **ONLY use libraries in go.mod**
- **Use GORM for database operations**
- **Use go-playground/validator for validation**

### Code Quality
- Follow patterns from existing modules
- Use proper error handling
- Implement validation
- Add comments for complex logic
- Use meaningful variable names

## 📋 Checklist Before Making Changes

### For New Modules
- [ ] Check `/docs/folder-structure.md` for organization
- [ ] Read `/docs/coding-standards.md` for patterns
- [ ] Review similar existing modules
- [ ] Follow naming conventions
- [ ] Implement proper error handling
- [ ] Add validation
- [ ] Update routes configuration

### For Existing Code
- [ ] Maintain consistency with existing patterns
- [ ] Follow established naming conventions
- [ ] Use same error handling approach
- [ ] Keep same response format
- [ ] Update documentation if needed

## 🚫 What NOT to Do

- ❌ Don't use different frameworks (only Go Fiber)
- ❌ Don't add new external libraries without approval
- ❌ Don't use English for error messages
- ❌ Don't ignore existing patterns
- ❌ Don't skip validation
- ❌ Don't forget error handling

